WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.113
Select each configuration and compare the values.

2
00:00:04.113 --> 00:00:15.528
In this source snapshot, both 32-bit examples disable the memory management unit, supervisor and user modes, atomics and floating point.

3
00:00:15.528 --> 00:00:22.159
Their issue widths differ: CV32A60X has one issue port, while CV32A65X has two.

4
00:00:22.159 --> 00:00:28.034
The 64-bit example enables the listed application-oriented facilities.

5
00:00:28.034 --> 00:00:31.811
Notice that commit width is a separate value.

6
00:00:31.811 --> 00:00:41.044
The configuration builder can override a raw package field: it gives the superscalar example two commit ports.

7
00:00:41.044 --> 00:00:47.339
Always read the selected package together with derived configuration logic.

8
00:00:47.339 --> 00:00:56.740
These are source-level capability limits; actual instruction throughput still depends on the program and stalls.

